WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.290
- You've been saving money

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:04.500
for down payment on a new car, exciting.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.820
You applied for an auto loan

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:09.030
with one bank and was denied, bummer.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:09.960
Another bank approved you,

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.950
but with an interest rate of 16%, yikes.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.680
Both lenders say that you
don't have enough credit.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.130
- Having no credit is different
from having bad credit.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.920
It doesn't mean you
necessarily did anything wrong.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.630
Maybe you don't like to borrow money,

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.820
maybe you just never got a credit card,

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.560
but from the lender's point of view,

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.630
you are a total mystery.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.670
They have no idea whether
you're the kind of person

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:33.990
who pays their bills on time,

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:36.780
so it's safer for them
just to turn you down.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.210
- Unfortunately, the
only way to build credit

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:40.410
is to use credit,

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.780
and the only way to use
credit is to get credit,

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.180
and the easiest way to
get credit is to already

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.710
have a credit history.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.530
- That sounds like a catch
22, but there are ways

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:51.780
to start building your
credit from scratch.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.300
It can take an investment
in time and money,

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.330
but if you ever want to buy
a house or get a car loan,

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.669
the process is definitely worth it.

00:00:59.669 --> 00:01:02.171
(upbeat electronic music)

00:01:02.171 --> 00:01:03.605
(coins clanging)

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:07.105
(upbeat electronic music)

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.260
- The best start would be to establish

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.180
a revolving line of credit

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.010
where how much you pay back each month

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:18.030
depends on how much you use,
in other words, a credit card.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:21.390
Many lenders have
pre-qualification applications

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.680
which allows you to apply

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.960
without a hard pull on your credit.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.130
This is a great option

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.590
if you're not sure whether you'll qualify

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.780
and don't wanna make your credit worse.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.330
Keep in mind, if you
qualify and move forward

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:36.540
with an official application,
the inquiry will be reported

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.180
and may temporarily
affect your credit score.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.700
- You may qualify for
an unsecured credit card

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.650
which gives you a specific spending limit.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.020
But if you're starting
without any credit history,

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.600
you'll probably have to
go for a secured card.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.670
This type of card requires collateral

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.070
in the form of a deposit,
which sets your credit limit.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:56.040
In other words, you
give the bank say $1,000

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.950
and they give you a credit
card with $1,000 limit.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.930
While there are a number of secured cards

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.110
that eventually graduate
to unsecured, others don't,

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.990
so be sure to do your research
before taking the leap.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.270
- Now, this may not sound much like credit

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.580
since you're essentially
borrowing your own money,

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.700
but it's a way to show the
bank that you're reliable.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.500
And the two main things they're looking at

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.140
are payment history and utilization.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.090
- Payment history weighs the most

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.440
when it comes to credit score.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.730
So it's imperative that you
pay all of your bills on time.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.040
If you miss your due date,
you'll incur a late fee,

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.050
but lenders will not
report your late payment

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.010
to the credit bureau

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:36.000
until you're more than 30
days past due, tick-tock.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.850
- Utilization is how much
credit you have available

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:42.270
on your card in relation to
how much you currently owe.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:46.050
So if you have $1,000 limit
and you've borrowed $500,

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:49.020
you have a 50% utilization rate.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.260
The lower your utilization,
the better you look to lenders

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.320
because it suggests you have
discipline and self-control

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.570
and don't run up cards to their limit.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:58.830
For optimal results,

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:02.940
try to keep your utilization
percentage below 30%.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.100
- But payment history and utilization

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.410
aren't the only things
that credit bureaus look at

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:08.760
when calculating your score.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.850
- They also factor in the
length of your credit history,

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:15.150
credit mix and inquiries and new accounts.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.180
- There's not much you can do
about length of credit history

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.240
except to get the process
started as soon as you can.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.220
Credit mix refers to having

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.260
a healthy balance of revolving credit,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.690
like credit cards, and installment credit,

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:30.480
like mortgages, car
loans, and student loans.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.120
Now, should you go take out a big car loan

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.350
just to build credit?

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:37.500
No way, it's never a
good idea to go into debt

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.810
for something you don't absolutely need.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.730
However, there is a safer option

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:43.740
to achieving a good credit mix.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:47.130
- Credit builder loans are
designed for exactly this purpose

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.770
to help consumers with no credit history

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.720
boost their credit worthiness.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.100
They're like savings accounts

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.800
and installment lines of credit combined.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.890
You choose your loan
amount and term length,

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.810
but instead of giving the money to you,

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.960
the lender puts it in a
special savings account.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.250
Once you've paid it off,

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.230
you get the total amount of the loan

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.910
minus a small amount of interest,

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.040
kind of like a loan in reverse.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.240
What's great about it is

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.310
that your monthly payments are reported

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.710
as traditional installment payments,

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:18.630
so you're building your credit history

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:21.240
and getting some motivation to save money.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.680
- There is a bit of a shortcut

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.150
to building credit from scratch

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:27.120
and that's to piggyback
off someone else's credit.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.660
The official term is called
becoming an authorized user,

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.190
which means they're allowing you

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:33.660
to use their line of credit

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.460
and your activity there will be reflected

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.230
on your credit reports.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.000
You'll often see this with spouses

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.870
or other family members helping
each other build credit.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:44.070
If the person giving you a piggyback ride

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:47.190
has low utilization and
a good payment history,

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:49.560
this can help your credit tremendously,

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.230
but they are risking their
own credit score to help you,

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:53.970
so don't abuse that.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:56.550
- Oh, there's one more
component of credit scores

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:57.690
that we haven't discussed

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.600
and that's inquiries and new accounts.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.450
Even though this factor is at
the bottom of the totem pole,

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:07.290
it can make quite the difference
if not managed properly.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.290
Every time you officially
apply for a line of credit,

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.330
your score takes a short-term ding,

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.340
whether or not you're even approved.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.830
If you apply blindly to lots of lenders

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.920
in a short period of time,
that can give the impression

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.360
that you're thirsty for debt,

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.000
and that's a huge red
flag in lenders' eyes.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.580
- [Philip] For someone with
no history or a bad score,

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.160
the world of credit can
feel like an exclusive party

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.690
that you're not invited to.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:32.400
- But it is possible to get in,

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.470
you just have to prove you know the rules.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.500
It takes time and discipline,
but it's so worth it.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.750
- And whether you're building
credit history from scratch

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.970
or rebuilding from past mistakes,

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.700
understanding how credit
reporting and scoring works

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.087
is an essential component.

00:05:46.087 --> 00:05:48.387
- [Philip and Julia] And
that's our two cents.

